A prover can establish a global fact while exposing only a carefully randomized local view. This guided notebook moves from exact simulation to algebraic soundness and constant-query verification.

## 1. Hide the names, preserve the relation

In the graph three-coloring protocol, a random permutation erases the semantic identity of the colors but preserves whether two endpoint colors differ. Explore how every distinct witness pair produces the same six-point law.

