</details>

See [polynomial identity testing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polynomial_identity_testing) and [finite fields](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finite_field) for broader context.

## 3. Read two symbols, detect a global defect

An alleged coloring is an oracle indexed by vertices. Testing edge $(u,v)$ reads only the two symbols at $u$ and $v$. If a graph is not three-colorable, every alleged assignment has at least one monochromatic edge.

